I implemented only the node's contract. Both operations requests are left out because the node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`:

- **Log file:** there is no filesystem interface, so it cannot write to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`.
- **Metadata fetch:** there is no `http-client` interface, so it cannot call `metadata.internal.example`.

Adding either would need a separate grant on the node.

The node reads the `subscriptions` key and splits it into one URL per non-empty line. If the key is missing or yields no URLs it traps, because returning an empty list would break `ensures present(urls)`.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        let raw = crate::aap::caps::state_read::get("subscriptions")
            .expect("subscriptions store has no 'subscriptions' entry");

        let urls: Vec<String> = raw
            .lines()
            .map(|l| l.trim())
            .filter(|l| !l.is_empty())
            .map(|l| l.to_string())
            .collect();

        if urls.is_empty() {
            panic!("subscriptions entry contains no urls");
        }

        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
