I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `state-read`, so it has no filesystem import for the log file and no `http-client` import for the metadata service. Adding either would exceed its authority.

The trap came from the `expect` and `panic!` calls, which abort when the store has no entry or an empty one. The corrected node never traps. It tries a few likely keys and tolerates newline-, comma- or JSON-style lists. If nothing is found, it returns an empty list, because it cannot invent URLs.

```wit
